// in GameSource/Graphics/BrnRendererMemory.cpp:207-210. Being Xenos microcode
// inside the guest image they have no PC counterpart and nothing in the
// converted asset tree supplies one.
//
// These four arrays are the SAME four programs recompiled for D3D9. There is no
// TUB source for them, so they were AUTHORED from the Xenos decode, the same
// route the corona, sun-corona, post-fx and Godray shaders took:
//     tools/assets/shaders/brn_im2dblit.fx
//     (entries mainIm2dDepthBlitVS / mainIm2dDepthBlitPS /
//      mainIm2dCompositeBlitVS / mainIm2dCompositeBlitPS)
// Every ALU line in that .fx carries the instruction number of its counterpart
// in the disassembly (tools/assets/shaders/xenos.py), and the .fx banner spells
// out the TWO deliberate PC deviations in the composite pixel program -- the
// scene term re-associated onto the D3D9 blend unit (a texture cannot be
// sampled while it is the bound render target) and the alpha lane left unwritten
// (this backend carries the motion-blur mask there). Read that banner before
// changing anything here.
//
// The constant surface is the CTAB interned in the console packages themselves
// (tools/assets/shaders/ctab.py). The console tables are
//     depth     vertex : gOffsetXYZ c0, gRightUp c1
//     depth     pixel  : DiffuseSampler s0
//     composite vertex : gOffsetXYZ c0, gRightUp c1, gUVOffsets c2, gUVScales c3
